From: "Jeremy D. Miller" <jeremy@jasperfx.net>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 08:32:58 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Discover Bobcat step definitions alongside Reqnroll and
 SpecFlow

Bobcat (https://github.com/JasperFx/bobcat) declares steps with the same
attribute names as Reqnroll in its own namespace - Bobcat.GivenAttribute,
WhenAttribute, ThenAttribute - plus Bobcat.CheckAttribute, a Then whose method
returns a bool. It has no [Binding]: a class that declares steps is a step
class. Until now the plugin saw none of it, because both step caches gate on
Reqnroll/SpecFlow CLR names and on [Binding].

- ReqnrollAttributeHelper: add the Bobcat.* names to the Given/When/Then
  arrays (Check maps to Then), a Check short name for the source path, and
  IsStepAttribute / IsStepAttributeShortName / CanContainBobcatSteps.
  GetAttributeClrName still generates Reqnroll.* for the create-step quick fix.
  GetAttributeStepKind returns null for Bobcat attributes so the "method name
  does not match pattern" inspection, which enforces Reqnroll's GivenXxx naming
  convention, does not fire on fixtures that never had it.
- AssemblyStepDefinitionCache: a type with no [Binding] is admitted when it
  declares steps, but only in an assembly that is or references Bobcat, so no
  other referenced assembly pays for a per-method scan. The class entry records
  whether a [Binding] was present instead of hard-coding true.
- ReqnrollStepsDefinitionsCache: a class with no [Binding] is admitted when it
  declares steps, by the same short-name rule the method walk already uses
  (attribute types cannot be resolved while the cache is being built). Cache
  version bumped to 16 since the population rule changed.
- Tests for the helper; changelog entry.

Reqnroll and SpecFlow behaviour is unchanged: same names, same [Binding] gate,
same generated attributes. The two deliberate widenings are that a class that
declares steps without [Binding] is now indexed (the plugin already admitted
any partial class on the same terms), and that a [Check("...")] attribute on a
method is read as a Then by short name in source, as [Given]/[When]/[Then]
already are.
